English translation (for convenience; the Chinese text governs)

PREAMBLE. This work is a unofficial clean-room remake and technical-preservation project of Flame Dragon 2: Legend of Golden Castle, made for cultural
preservation. The copyright holder wants it widely used, discussed and shown,
while keeping its commercial rights. This license is built accordingly:
non-commercial use is free and permissive; commercial use is reserved for a
separate agreement with the copyright holder.

1. DEFINITIONS.
   (a) "Work" means everything in this repository authored by the copyright
       holder, including source code, build and packaging scripts, tools,
       documentation, specifications, disassembly notes, file-format analyses,
       translations, name tables and revision records, font renderings and
       theme assets made by the copyright holder, Contributions incorporated
       under Section 7, and compiled or packaged forms of any of these. Theme
       assets extracted or converted from Original Assets are not part of the
       Work; they are Original Assets.
   (b) "Original Assets" means the original game's executables, data files,
       artwork, maps, tiles, portraits, music, sound effects, bitmap fonts and
       game text, and their counterparts in any other platform version.
       Original Assets belong to the original game's respective rights holders or their respective rights holders.
   (c) "Modified Version" means any work based on the Work through
       modification, translation, porting, extension or combination.
   (d) "Commercial Use" means use aimed at obtaining money or other
       consideration, directly or indirectly, including without limitation:
       selling the Work or a Modified Version; offering it for a fee, by
       subscription or membership; bundling it with goods, hardware or
       services; adding advertising, in-app purchases or sponsorship
       placements; using it in the operations, products or services of a
       for-profit entity; and using it in commercial exhibitions, events or
       marketing.
   (e) "Contribution" means anything intentionally submitted to the copyright
       holder for inclusion in the Work: code, documentation, translations,
       assets and proposed changes.

2. SCOPE AND EXCLUSIONS.
   (a) This license applies only to the Work.
   (b) This license does not apply to Original Assets. The Work does not
       distribute them; users must supply their own lawfully obtained copy of
       the original game. The copyright holder claims no rights in Original
       Assets and cannot license them.
   (c) For documentation, research and demonstration this repository contains
       small excerpts that include Original Assets: original-versus-remake comparison screenshots, asset contact sheets, and small font or file-format research extracts. The Original-Asset portions of
       these excerpts are outside this license and are included for research
       and commentary. Translations and measured tables authored by the
       copyright holder are part of the Work and are licensed under these
       terms to the extent of the copyright holder's rights in them; the
       translations are derivative of the original text, and using them to
       run the game still requires the user's own original copy.
   (d) Third-party components in this repository or its packages (for example
       Go modules, Ebiten and AppImage runtime components)
       are provided under their own licenses, which are distributed with them,
       and are not governed by this license.

3. NON-COMMERCIAL GRANT. Subject to Section 5, anyone may, free of charge and
   without prior permission:
   (a) use, run, reproduce and distribute the Work for personal, educational,
       research, preservation, commentary or other non-commercial purposes;
   (b) make Modified Versions and distribute them under this license on the
       same non-commercial condition; whoever distributes a Modified Version
       agrees to license their own changes to others on the same terms as
       this license;
   (c) make translations or language packs and distribute them under this
       license on the same non-commercial condition.

4. EXPRESSLY PERMITTED SHOWCASE AND COVERAGE. The following are not
   Commercial Use under Section 1(d) even if they generate income, and are
   expressly permitted:
   (a) streaming, recording, broadcasting, reviewing, teaching or reporting
       on the Work or a Modified Version, including earning advertising
       revenue, viewer donations or membership income under the ordinary
       rules of platforms such as YouTube, Twitch or Bilibili;
   (b) quoting, showing or discussing the Work — including screenshots, code
       excerpts and documentation — in articles, books, academic papers,
       talks, exhibitions or courses;
   (c) showing or providing the Work at preservation, academic, non-profit or
       community events.
   Attribution under Section 5(b) applies. The following remain Commercial
   Use and are not covered by this Section: selling the Work or a Modified
   Version as the main object of sale; packaging it as a paid product or
   service; and using it as a marketing tool or demonstration content for
   other goods, hardware or services.

5. CONDITIONS.
   (a) Keep this license and the copyright notice in every distribution of
       the Work or a Modified Version.
   (b) When publicly distributing, showing or transmitting the Work or a
       Modified Version, give reasonable and visible credit: the name of the
       Work, the copyright holder (Wang Chun-Yu / wicanr2), and the original
       source at https://github.com/wicanr2/fd2_re .
   (c) When distributing a Modified Version, state clearly that it is
       modified, what was changed and by whom. Do not imply that it comes
       from or is endorsed by the copyright holder, and do not use the
       copyright holder's name or the Work's name in a confusing way.
   (d) Do not charge for obtaining or using the Work or a Modified Version
       itself (actual cost of physical media and shipping excepted), and do
       not exchange them for other consideration. Income permitted by
       Section 4 is not restricted by this paragraph.
   (e) Do not distribute Original Assets, and do not bundle them with the
       Work.
   (f) Do not remove, obscure or alter copyright, license or attribution
       notices in the Work.
   (g) Do not circumvent this license. Works produced by automated
       conversion, reformatting, rewriting or translation into another
       programming language remain Modified Versions bound by this license.

6. RESERVED RIGHTS AND COMMERCIAL LICENSING.
   (a) All rights not expressly granted are reserved. Commercial Use requires
       prior written permission from the copyright holder.
   (b) The copyright holder may license the Work to anyone on terms other
       than this license, including commercial and exclusive terms. Such
       licenses do not affect non-commercial rights others have already
       obtained under this license.
   (c) Commercial enquiries: wicanr2@gmail.com. Enquiries are welcome — this
       Section exists to keep commercial terms negotiable, not to refuse
       cooperation.

7. CONTRIBUTIONS.
   (a) By submitting a Contribution, the contributor grants the copyright
       holder a perpetual, irrevocable, worldwide, royalty-free,
       sublicensable license to use, reproduce, modify and distribute the
       Contribution in any way, and to license it as part of the Work under
       this license or any other terms, including commercial terms.
   (b) The contributor warrants that they are entitled to grant that license
       and that the Contribution contains no unlicensed Original Assets or
       third-party material.
   (c) Contributors keep copyright in their Contributions; the copyright
       holder will credit contributors in the project records where
       reasonable.
   (d) Do not submit a Contribution if you do not accept this Section.

8. NAMES. "《炎龍騎士團 2》反向工程與重製", "Flame Dragon 2 Reverse Engineering and Remake" and this
   repository's name identify the Work. A Modified Version may state that it
   is based on the Work, but may not use the same or a confusingly similar
   name as its own name without the copyright holder's written consent.

9. NO WARRANTY; LIMITATION OF LIABILITY. THE WORK IS PROVIDED "AS IS",
   WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED
   TO MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NON-INFRINGEMENT.
   TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, THE COPYRIGHT HOLDER IS NOT LIABLE
   FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY ARISING FROM THE WORK OR ITS USE,
   NOR FOR THE LAWFULNESS OF THE USER'S ACQUISITION OR USE OF ORIGINAL ASSETS.

10. TERMINATION AND REINSTATEMENT.
   (a) Rights under this license terminate automatically for anyone who
       breaches it.
   (b) If the breach is cured within thirty days of becoming aware of it and
       the copyright holder is notified, the license is reinstated as of the
       date of cure.
   (c) The copyright holder may refuse reinstatement for distributing
       Original Assets (Section 5(e)) or for unauthorised Commercial Use
       (Section 6(a)).
   (d) Termination does not affect the rights of others who received copies
       of the Work from the breaching party in good faith, as long as they
       themselves comply with this license.

11. GOVERNING LAW AND VENUE. This license is governed by the laws of the
   Republic of China (Taiwan). The Taiwan Taipei District Court is the court
   of first instance for disputes arising from it. The Traditional Chinese
   text governs; in case of discrepancy, the Traditional Chinese text
   prevails over any translation.

12. RELATIONSHIP TO THE ORIGINAL RIGHTS HOLDER. The Work is not affiliated
   with, endorsed, sponsored or licensed by the original game's respective rights holders; it is an independent
   third-party preservation and research project. The copyright holder
   reserves the right to adjust the Work's contents in response to a lawful
   claim by the original rights holder.

13. VERSIONS. The copyright holder may publish new versions of RRSAL
   (identified by version number; this is version 1.0).
   Rights obtained under a given version remain governed by that version; a
   new version applies to copies of the Work distributed after its
   publication.
